  'responsible-gaming': {
    slug: 'responsible-gaming', title: 'Responsible Gaming: Limits, Risk & 18+ Guidance', description: 'Read clear responsible-gaming guidance about 18+ access, financial loss, time and spending limits, breaks and chasing losses.', eyebrow: 'Play within clear limits', h1: 'Responsible Gaming Guide', intro: 'Gaming with paid entries can cause financial loss. No game, bonus or strategy can guarantee a win. This website is intended only for users aged 18 and above.',
    sections: [
      { heading: 'Only for users aged 18+', paragraphs: ['Do not create or use a paid gaming account if you are under 18. Age requirements and gaming laws can differ by state and location. Check the rules that apply where you live.', 'Do not use another person’s identity or payment account to avoid an age or location check. Account availability does not prove that participation is legal in every place.'] },
      { heading: 'Set a spending limit', paragraphs: ['Decide the maximum amount you can afford to lose before you start. Use only money left after rent, food, education, healthcare, bills, savings and debt payments. Treat the limit as final.', 'Never borrow money or use household funds for gaming. Keep a simple record of deposits, withdrawals and total spending so you can see the real result.'], bullets: ['Use only an amount you can afford to lose', 'Set a daily or weekly spending limit', 'Keep household money separate', 'Never borrow to play', 'Review your transaction record'] },
      { heading: 'Set a time limit and take breaks', paragraphs: ['Choose a fixed time to stop before you open a game. Use a phone alarm if needed. Take regular breaks and do not continue late at night because you feel one more round will change the result.', 'Stop for the day if gaming affects sleep, work, study, relationships or mood. A break is more useful than making quick decisions while angry or worried.'] },
      { heading: 'Never chase a loss', paragraphs: ['Chasing a loss means spending more because you want to recover an earlier loss. It can increase harm quickly. A previous result does not make the next result more likely to help you.', 'Ignore “fixed game”, “sure-shot trick”, “100% winning strategy” and guaranteed-profit claims. Do not pay for prediction groups, bots or account-control services.'] },
      { heading: 'Use account controls when available', paragraphs: ['Open Account or Settings and look for deposit limits, time reminders, a cooling-off option, account closure or self-exclusion. Use any control that helps you take a break or stop.', 'You can also open customer support and ask which account-limit or closure options are available. Keep the request number and do not share your password or OTP.'] },
      { heading: 'When to seek help', paragraphs: ['Stop and speak to someone you trust if gaming causes debt, stress, secrecy, arguments or repeated failed attempts to stop. You can also contact a qualified mental-health, financial-counselling or gaming-support service in your area.', 'If there is an immediate risk to your safety, contact local emergency help.'] },
    ], related: [{ label: 'Disclaimer', href: '/disclaimer' }, { label: 'Games overview', href: '/shree-win-games' }, { label: 'Promotion guide', href: '/shree-win-promotion' }],
  },
